1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alessandro_Cesarini_(XVII_secolo)
2 CONT
2 CONT Alessandro Cesarini ( Rome , 1592 - Rome , 25 January 1644 ) was an Italian Catholic cardinal and bishop .
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Of the family of the dukes of Civitanova and marquises of Civita Lavinia , he was the son of Giuliano II Cesarini (1572-1613), duke of Civitanova and Montecosaro, and of Livia Orsini . His great-uncle was Cardinal Alessandro Cesar
2 CONC ini senior (who died in 1542 ). Other cardinals in the family were Giuliano Cesarini (created in 1426 by Pope Martin V ) and Giuliano Cesarini iuniore (created in 1493 by Pope Alexander VI ).
2 CONT
2 CONT After studying in Parma , he became a cleric of the Apostolic Chamber and was governor in the conclave of 1623 , in which Pope Urban VIII was elected .
2 CONT
2 CONT He was created cardinal-deacon in the consistory of 30 August 1627 with the diaconia of Santa Maria in Domnica ; in 1632 he opted for the diaconate of Saints Cosmas and Damian .
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1636 he was appointed bishop of Viterbo ; the following year he opted for the diaconia of Santa Maria in Cosmedin , then, in 1638 , for that of Saint Eustace . In the same year he renounced the government of the diocese.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in Rome in 1644 . He was buried in the family tomb in the church of Santa Maria in Aracoeli .
