2 CONT -------------------------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from <http://www.usinternet.com/users/dfnels/lemaitre.htm>:
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Lemaitre-Auge-Dueme: (1666-aft.1734)
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Francois Lemaitre-Auger & Juditha Rigault, baptized at Perrot, Quebec. He married Madeleine Crevier dit Bellerive (1670-1746) (daughter of Nicolas Crevier & Louise Leloutre) at Cap-de-la-Madeleine, Champlain, Que
2 CONC bec in 1689. Their children were Marie-Francoise (b.1691) (m.Charles Paille in 1710), Charles II (bap.1694), Etienne-Charles (b.1695), Catherine (b.1697) (m.Francois Lefebvre in 1719), Michel (b.1701) (m.Marie-Charlotte Trottier-V
2 CONC alcour in 1727),
2 CONT Madeleine (b.1702) (m.Pierre Lefebvre-Descoteaux in 1723), Jean Bte. (b.1704) (m.1st.to Francoise Lesieur in 1727 & m.2nd.to Marie Anne Fafard in 1733), Francois (b.1705) (m.1st.to Charlotte Guignard in 1733 & m.2nd.to Marie-Anne 
2 CONC Dulignon de Lamirande in 1750), Marie-Josephe (b.1707) (m.Joseph Fafard in 1729), Josephte (b.1710) & Marie-Anne-Alexis (b.1712) (m.Jean Bte.Heron in 1732).
2 CONT
2 CONT July 1713 - Charles Lemaistre-Auge & Jean Dulignon were hired for the west (8ta8ois).
2 CONT 1723 - Charles & Estienne Lemaitre dit Auger are hired by Charles Nolan for Michilimackinac.
