1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Louis Marie Celeste d'Aumont, duc de Piennes, afterwards duc d'Aumont (1762–1831), emigrated during the Revolution and served in the army of the royalists, as also in the Swedish army. During the Hundred Days he ef
2 CONC fected a descent upon Normandy in the Bourbon interest, and succeeded in capturing Bayeux and Caen. He was a gentilhomme of the Chamber under Louis XVIII, after the Restauration.
