1 CONT
1 CONT - 19 April 1725 Notary: F. Lepailleur de LaFerté (Mtl) 
1 CONT Transfer of a sum of money; by Maurice Mesnard, interpreter, to François-Marie Bouat, counsellor of the King and lieutenant general at the royal court of law of Montreal 
1 CONT
1 CONT - 12 May 1725 Notary: F. Lepailleur de LaFerté (Mtl) 
1 CONT Company between Maurice Blondeau, bourgeois merchant, of the city of Villemarie, and Maurice Mesnard, interpreter of Ottawa languages for the King 
1 CONT
1 CONT - 20 July 1731 Notary: R. Chorel de Saint-Romain (Mtl) 
1 CONT Enlistement of Gabriel Grou, of the Côte de Vertus in the Island of Montreal, to Maurice Menard, interpreter and sergeant of the troops of the Navy of Michillimakinac 
1 CONT
1 CONT - 25 July 1731 Notary: J.B. Adhémar dit Saint-Martin 
1 CONT Enlistement as a qualified trapper of Joseph Baron, of the Côte des Vertus and of Charles Laviolette, of the Côte de Notre Dame de Liesse in the Island of Montreal, to Maurice Mesnard, interpreter in Ottawa languages 
1 CONT
1 CONT - 26 July 1731 Notary: R. Chorel de Saint-Romain (Mtl) 
1 CONT Sale of part of the land situated in the seignory of Bourgerville; by Maurice Menard, interpreter at the Michillimakinac Post, to Françoise Lamoureux of St Jermain, bourgeois merchant of the city of Montreal 
1 CONT
1 CONT - 26 July 1731 Notary: R. Chorel de Saint-Romain (Mtl) 
1 CONT Enlistement of Joseph Majort, of the parish of Vertus in the Island of Montreal, to Maurice Menard, interpreter and sergeant of the Navy troops, of the Missillimakina Post 
1 CONT
1 CONT - 21 Jan 1736 Notary: F. Lepailleur de LaFerté (Mtl) 
1 CONT Release; by Maurice Menard, interpreter at the Misilimakinac Post, to Charles Nolan dit Lamarque, bourgeois merchant, of Montreal, accepting by Pierre Neveu, his assistant 
1 CONT
1 CONT - 12 Aug 1736 Refer to the Marriage Contract of François Menard, same date
1 CONT
1 CONT - 2 June 1742 Notary: C.C.J. Porlier (Mtl) 
1 CONT Deposition of a receipt from François Raine, counsellor to the King and chief clerk of the Superior Counsel of Québec, widower of Louise Bouate, his spouse, as well as in her name acting on behalf ot he co-inheritors of the deceas
1 CONC ed François-Marie Bouate, to Maurice Mesnard, interpreter of foreign languages 
1 CONT
1 CONT Reference: http://www.geninfo.org/metis/interpretes.html 
1 CONT
1 CONT ****************************************************
1 CONT
1 CONT From: http://www.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~sdlyman/Families/mesnard.htm
1 CONT
1 CONT Maurice Menard dit LaFontaine was born June 06, 1664 in Trois-Rivières, Maurice, Québec and was Christened June 7, 1664 in Trois-Rivières, St. Maurice, Québec. He was the son of Jacques Ménard and Catherine Forestier. Maurice was 
1 CONC an interpreter and Fur Trader at Fort Michillimakinac. Maurice married Madeleine Couc LaFleur on October 1681, at the Mission St. Ignace, Fort Michillimakinac, Michigan. She was the daughter of Pierre Couc-LaFleur and Marie Miteou
1 CONC amigoukoue. Maurice Ménard died May 9, 1741 at Chambly, Québec. 
1 CONT
1 CONT ****************************************************
